  "body": "The docs site has no search: `site/config.toml` sets `build_search_index = false`. Turn it on and add a search box to the templates (`site/templates/base.html`), using Zola's built-in elasticlunr index or a lighter JS index. It must stay a static site with no server and no third-party service.\n\nCheck it works on GitHub Pages under the `/Camcraft` base path, on a phone-width screen, and in light and dark themes if the site has them.\n\nDone means: the published site has a search box in the header, and searching \"refused\", \"WCS\" or \"adaptive\" finds the right pages.\n",
